# AGENTS.md

The {{ project_name }} meta-repository. It holds the shared agent rules, OpenSpec with sdd-kit, decisions and checks. The application code lives in the clones in `repos/`, listed in `repos.toml`; each clone has its own git, branches and rules.

Start the agent from the root of this repository, also for a task in a single clone. The `.claude/` settings and the sdd-kit hooks work only when started from the root ([docs/agents/repository-layout.md](docs/agents/repository-layout.md)).

## Language

- Everything in this repository is written in {{ language_name }}: documents, OpenSpec artifacts including clarifying questions, code comments, test messages, task descriptions, command output meant for people, commit messages and pull requests.
- Code identifiers, file and command names stay in English, and so do the keywords and headings that sdd-kit's checks parse.
- Files managed by sdd-kit (`openspec/protocols/`, `openspec/schemas/`, `openspec/tooling/`, the `openspec-*` skills, `.claude/commands/` and `.claude/agents/`) are never translated or edited by hand.

## Planning

- Every OpenSpec change is planned, tracked and archived in the root `openspec/`, even if it touches one clone. Only code and tests stay in the clones ([ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-planning-in-root-openspec.md)).
- Small edits can be made without OpenSpec, in the meta-repository or directly in a clone, with a branch and a pull request.
- An `openspec/` folder inside a clone is not changed from the root.
- sdd-kit is installed with `mise run kit:install` and updated with `mise run kit:update`; its files are committed ([docs/agents/tooling.md](docs/agents/tooling.md)).

## Branches

- In every clone `main` is production and the rest branch (`ref` in `repos.toml`, usually `dev`) is the test server. Each clone follows its branch model, main-based or dev-based:

<!-- repos:begin:branches -->

No repositories yet; each repository added with `mise run add-repo` gets its rule here.

<!-- repos:end:branches -->

- A main-based work branch is never merged into the rest branch directly, only through a pull request. Conflicts with the rest branch go through a merge branch `merge/<name>-into-<rest branch>`; fixes after review or QA go on the work branch.
- At rest a clone is on its rest branch. Before each new ticket or task, and before creating its branch, run `mise run pull` and `mise run status`.
- A meta-repository working branch is created from an updated `main`. The meta-repository's `main` changes only through a pull request.
- Git commands run in the folder of the repository they concern: `git -C repos/<name> ...`. In the root, `git` refers only to the meta-repository itself.
{%- if agent_git_default == 'on' %}
- The agent commits and pushes by default; each developer can turn either off for themselves. The agent never commits or pushes to `main`. The hook `.claude/hooks/agent-git-guard.mjs` checks this ([docs/agents/agent-settings.md](docs/agents/agent-settings.md)).
{%- else %}
- The agent commits and pushes only if the developer enabled it for themselves; by default both are forbidden. The agent never commits or pushes to `main`. The hook `.claude/hooks/agent-git-guard.mjs` checks this ([docs/agents/agent-settings.md](docs/agents/agent-settings.md)).
{%- endif %}
- The agent never merges a pull request and never merges into `main`, `dev` or a rest branch in any repository; the developer merges by hand.
- No Claude attribution in commit messages, pull request titles, descriptions or comments, in any repository. The hook refuses it.
- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits.

Details in [docs/agents/branches.md](docs/agents/branches.md).
{%- if tracker != 'none' %}

## {{ tracker_name }} and tickets

- {{ tracker_name }} is read-only for the agent: it reads tickets, comments, status and attachments and changes nothing in {{ tracker_name }}.
- Unclear ticket points go to the developer in the chat, in the ticket's language as a numbered list, one short question per line, with nothing before or after it. The developer posts them to the ticket.
- When the work of a ticket's OpenSpec change is done and checked, the agent opens the pull request itself, if agent commit and push are enabled.

Details, including pull request titles, in [docs/agents/ticket-workflow.md](docs/agents/ticket-workflow.md).
{%- else %}

## Pull requests

- When the work of an OpenSpec change is done and checked, the agent opens the pull request itself, if agent commit and push are enabled.

Details, including pull request titles, in [docs/agents/ticket-workflow.md](docs/agents/ticket-workflow.md).
{%- endif %}

## Clone rules

- Before editing a file in a clone, read the clone's own rules: its `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/` and `README.md`, whichever exist. A clone's `CLAUDE.md` may be absent from git and exist only on the developer's machine; read it when it is there.
- The clones' own git hooks run on a commit in a clone as usual. Do not bypass them with `--no-verify`.
- Clone edits are committed to the clone's repository. If an edit in a clone is desirable but not part of the current task, record it in [docs/clone-backlog.md](docs/clone-backlog.md).

## Commands

All commands run from the root. Each calls the clone's own command in its folder and returns its exit code. Run clone tests and checks with these commands. `mise run add-repo` creates the `mise run <name>:*` tasks as stubs; `/bootstrap` in Claude Code, or a developer, writes the clone's own command into `mise-tasks/<name>/`.

<!-- repos:begin:commands -->

No repositories yet. Add one with `mise run add-repo`; it creates the `mise run <name>:*` tasks.

<!-- repos:end:commands -->

### Meta-repository

| What | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Set up the machine | `mise run setup` |
| Add a repository | `mise run add-repo` |
| Regenerate the repository lists from `repos.toml` | `mise run repos:sync` |
| Clone the missing clones | `mise run clone` |
| Update the meta-repository and the clones | `mise run pull` |
| Clone branches and changes | `mise run status` |
| Single check of the clones | `mise run check` |
| Lint texts and agent settings | `mise run lint` |
| Meta-repository tests | `mise run test` |
| Install or update sdd-kit | `mise run kit:install`, `mise run kit:update` |

Developers write the environment files themselves; `setup` neither creates nor changes them ([docs/agents/environment.md](docs/agents/environment.md)).
{%- if e2e %}

## End-to-end tests

End-to-end browser tests that cover several clones together live in the root `e2e/` folder ([e2e/README.md](e2e/README.md)). The first feature that needs such tests creates the folder's setup. A clone's own browser tests stay in its clone.
{%- endif %}

## Checks

- A shared rule for clone code is an `ast-grep` rule with a test, not a line in this file. The procedure is in the `add-ast-grep-rule` skill.
- Fix a finding in a clone in the clone; do not weaken a meta-repository rule without discussion.
- `repos.toml` is the only list of repositories. After a hand edit run `mise run repos:sync`; `mise run check` fails while the lists disagree.
- Do not create `CLAUDE.md`, `CLAUDE.local.md` or `.claude/CLAUDE.md` in the root. Any of them stops Claude Code from reading this file ([ADR 0002](docs/adr/0002-only-agents-md.md)); `mise run lint` catches them.

